  "question": {
    "text": "A dipole with two electric charges of $2 \\mu \\mathrm{C}$ magnitude each, with separation distance $0.5 \\mu \\mathrm{~m}$, is placed between the plates of a capacitor such that its axis is parallel to an electric field established between the plates when a potential difference of 5 V is applied. Separation between the plates is 0.5 mm. If the dipole is rotated by $30^{\\circ}$ from the axis, it tends to realign in the direction due to a torque. The value of torque is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eIhl0",
      "text": "$5 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{Nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "p8ZMm",
      "text": "$5 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{Nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DfX06",
      "text": "$2.5 \\times 10^{-12} \\mathrm{Nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1dPsh",
      "text": "$2.5 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{Nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{E}=\\frac{\\mathrm{v}}{\\mathrm{~d}}=\\frac{5}{5 \\times 10^{-4}}=10^4 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{m} \\\\\n& \\tau=\\mathrm{PE} \\sin \\theta<br/>\\end{aligned}$<br/>Where $\\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{qa}=2 \\times 10^{-6} \\times 5 \\times 10^{-7}$<br/>$=1 \\times 10^{-12} \\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{m}$<br/>$\\tau=1 \\times 10^{-12} \\times 10^4 \\times \\frac{1}{2}=5 \\times 10^{-9} \\mathrm{~N}-\\mathrm{m}$",
    "image": null
  },
